      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The clinical and anatomo-pathological patterns of Crohn's ileitis are reported and the various etiopathogenetic hypotheses are briefly considered. The acute forms of Crohn's ileitis are then described: appendicular, peritonitic, occlusive and toxic forms. The study is based on 68 personal cases."},
